Andrew Spezowka (CIDA) as a representative of Donors Interest Group
• Under this second phase, the ESSP partnership has grown, firmly placing research as a public good in Ethiopia and making the necessary investments. – Ato Newai and his team at EDRI deserve full credit for advancing demand for evidence-based research for our collective benefit. • This symposium, and the policy conference that preceded it, could not have been better timed by EDRI and IFPRI. – Recently, the Government of Ethiopia has initiated the preparation of its next fiveyear development plan -- building on the accomplishments achieved under PASDEP. – Bringing together government policy-makers and planners, researchers, and development practitioners, EDRI and IFPRI have presented a body of high quality research to inform Ethiopia’s future development strategy. • Organizations such as EDRI, other think tanks and tertiary institutions have a vital role to play in working with government to ensure that development plans are based on the best available evidence of what’s working. • Our collective responsibility as donors is to be adaptive to the changes needed for Ethiopia to enjoy many more decades of economic growth for the well-being of all Ethiopians and for its neighbours.
